title: Display details
pid: 5d9f646a-21c2-4411-a7c6-9dbb97e4980c
body: |2-
  - Heralds conceal the metadata rather than covering it with a display
    overlay. With 'concealcursor=nc', entering insert mode on a line
    reveals its raw metadata (arguably clearer for editing); Emacs never
    revealed it. Semantics, colors and the server-owned rule table are
    identical.
  - Readable-ids shortens UUIDs by concealing the tail to an ellipsis
    and renders titles as inline virtual text; same behavior, same
    server round-trip, different mechanism.
  - Server messages name Emacs chords and Emacs commands. The client
    rewrites those it has a twin for, in the messages it shows and in
    the fork-confirmation buffer and the absent-reference warning
    ('with_neovim_bindings' in nvim/lua/skg/messages.lua, which reads
    the Neovim keys and Ex names from nvim/lua/skg/keymaps.lua): the chords
    C-c s e, C-c s w, C-c s s, C-c s r, C-c g RET, C-c g v, C-c v o, and the
    fork-confirmation buffer's C-c C-c and C-c C-k, which are
    '<localleader>cc' and '<localleader>ck' there; and the commands
    skg-restore-deleted-node, skg-restore-removed-membership,
    skg-investigate-unknown-node, skg-set-relRepo and
    skg-set-flag-search-matching, which become their ':Skg*' twins.
    Any other Emacs name a message carries stays as it is.
  - The fork confirmation: the server's notification ("N node(s) will
    be forked. Save again to approve, or kill this buffer to
    decline.") names no key. In Neovim the client asks at once
    ("Fork the listed node(s)?"); later, '<localleader>cc' in the
    confirmation buffer approves and '<localleader>ck' declines, while
    ':w' there refuses and names those two keys.
  - A view shown from a perspective other than its root homes
    (<localleader>vo, ':SkgCyclePerspective') is not marked by
    default: Emacs's mode name reads "SKG:the perspective of tracy",
    say, there,
    but the Neovim client draws no statusline, and setting one would
    override the user's. The perspective is 'b:skg_perspective'
    (its wire name, or unset) and its name
    'b:skg_perspective_name', and
    =%{v:lua.require'skg.buffer'.perspective_mode_line()}= in a
    'statusline' or 'winbar' shows ":the perspective of tracy", say,
    there. The
    message each switch shows names the perspective the buffer now
    shows.
  - View buffers are named 'skg://TITLE' (search: 'skg://?TERMS');
    Emacs used '*TITLE*'. Message/report buffers live under
    'skg://messages/...', 'skg://unknown-node', 'skg://diff-view: ...',
    etc.
